{
 "comment": "The terminal validation table's test vectors (docs/adr/0019 D9), shared by internal/facade (Go) and extensions/vscode (TypeScript). Each vector is a runInTerminal request's arguments as a debug adapter sends them; platform is posix (Linux, macOS), windows, or all; valid is whether eyedbg forwards it, else rule is the first rule it breaks (0: go-dap can't decode it, so it never reaches the facade). repeat, when set, fills a field before the check: title gets item repeated count times, args count copies of item appended, env count variables V1..VN set to item; itemRepeat (default 1) repeats item itself first. Keys are exact: case variants and duplicates are tested in Go only (the facade re-encodes what it checked).",
 "vectors": [
  {
   "name": "debugpy's request",
   "platform": "posix",
   "valid": true,
   "arguments": {
    "kind": "integrated",
    "title": "Python Debug Console",
    "cwd": "/home/u/proj",
    "args": [
     "/usr/bin/python3",
     "/opt/debugpy/launcher",
     "5678",
     "--",
     "/home/u/proj/app.py",
     "a b",
     "$HOME;echo x",
     "\"q\"",
     "`id`",
     "*",
     ""
    ],
    "env": {
     "DEBUGPY_LOG_DIR": null
    }
   }
  },
